  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "Which frequency the signal holds at each moment, and how strong it is",
        "amplitude[n] = the distance of z[n] from zero",
        "frequency[n] = the change of the angle of z[n], times rate / (2*pi)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "How the library gets there",
      "items": [
        "emd splits x[n] into modes, each of one frequency at a time",
        "hilbert gives z[n] = imf[n] + i*H{imf}[n] for each of them",
        "The answer is not a spectrum but a list of curves, one pair per mode"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What it rests on",
      "items": [
        "Each mode must hold one frequency at a time for any of this to mean something",
        "Where emd fails to separate them, that mode gives a mean of several",
        "That failure moves here unchanged, and nothing downstream can mend it"
      ]
    }
  ]
